  "brief": "AppLovin is reportedly in talks to acquire ad-tech firm Criteo in a deal that could target expansion in the retail media landscape.\n\nAppLovin / Criteo (Rumored): AppLovin and Criteo Deal Rumors. AppLovin is reportedly in talks to acquire ad-tech firm Criteo [3, 4, 6]. The deal is still in the early stages and no official announcement has been made [1, 2, 7]. The acquisition would potentially target expansion in the retail media landscape [3, 4, 6].\nTPG / Bill Holdings (Rumored): TPG and Bill Holdings Take-Private Deal Rumors. TPG is reportedly nearing a take-private deal for Bill Holdings [10, 11, 12]. The deal is rumored to be a take-private deal [9, 10, 11]. There is no new information on the deal [12].\nAir Water Ventures / Proud Source Water (Announced): Air Water Ventures to Acquire Proud Source Water. Air Water Ventures is acquiring Proud Source Water [13, 14, 15]. The deal is expected to close in 2027 [14]. The acquisition is valued at up to $150M [13].\nTransom Capital / SoundThinking (Completed): Transom Capital Acquires SoundThinking. Transom Capital has acquired SoundThinking, a public safety technology company [16, 17, 18]. The acquisition was completed after a tender offer for SoundThinking's shares [16, 17, 19]. The deal is now completed [16, 17, 18].\nonsemi / Synaptics (Pending approval): onsemi and Synaptics Deal. onsemi and Synaptics are acquiring each other [20, 21].\nDoorDash / Instacart (Announced): DoorDash to Acquire Instacart. DoorDash is acquiring Instacart in a $17 billion deal [26, 27, 28]. The deal has been announced and is currently under review by the DOJ [23]. The acquisition is expected to expand DoorDash's grocery delivery business [25, 24].\nICEYE / Avio (Announced): ICEYE and Avio Deal. ICEYE is acquiring Avio, an Italian rocket builder [30, 31, 32]. The deal is worth over €2 billion [30, 32]. The takeover bid was launched by ICEYE on November 17 [30, 31, 33].\nBASF / Evonik (Rumored): BASF and Evonik Deal Rumors. BASF is considering further concessions in its bid for Evonik [35, 36]. Evonik has rejected BASF's takeover bid, but left room for 'purely informational' talks [38, 40]. BASF has increased its bid for Evonik to over €11 billion [41].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Pursuit Industrial Holdings Acquires Berlin Manufacturer [42].\n- Canada must curb predatory private equity buyouts [43].\n- Oxo takeover bid gets good grip on tariff whiplash [44].",
